{% set local_problem %}
<p>Guntersville properties face a debris onslaught from all directions. Pine trees drop needles year-round. Hardwoods shed leaves every fall. The lake environment means additional organic matter blowing onto roofs. Without protection, gutters fill up fast.</p>

<p>For full-time residents, that means climbing ladders multiple times a year or paying for professional cleaning. Annoying, but manageable.</p>

<p>For vacation homes and rentals, it's more serious. Gutters can clog and overflow while you're away. By the time you discover the problem — or a renter calls to complain — water has been damaging your fascia, landscaping, or foundation for weeks. Emergency maintenance during peak rental season is expensive and frustrating.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this by keeping debris out automatically. Your gutters function properly whether you're there daily, visiting monthly, or hosting guests year-round.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters. They allow water to enter while blocking leaves, pine needles, and other debris. The debris either blows away or sits on top where it eventually dries and falls off.</p>

<p>For Guntersville's demanding environment, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards. The fine mesh blocks even small debris like pine needles and roof grit while handling heavy water flow during storms. The solid construction also holds up better in humid conditions than cheaper alternatives.</p>

<p>Combined with properly sized gutters and adequate downspouts, guards create a complete system that protects your lake home with minimal attention required.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed gutter guards on lake properties for over 20 years. We know which products hold up in this environment, which fail, and how to design systems that actually work for vacation homes and rentals.</p>

<p>Our goal is to give you gutters you don't have to think about. For lake property owners, that's worth a lot.</p>
